To map a repository and find call sites, use a read-only exploration subagent on a small model (Haiku) inside your own context, then act on the result.
exit 0
>>> notes identity --project demo 
The SessionStart hook (`qargi hook session-start`) appends `export QARGI_LEAD='ID'`, ID being the session id, to the file named by `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE`, so the later commands of the session know their lead identity. Tested by qargi: the line is written when `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` is set and `QARGI_LEAD` is not. Not verified: that Claude Code reads that file in a real session. Without it start the session with `QARGI_LEAD=ID` set: `feature`, `local`, `review` and `release` read it; only marshal verbs take `--as ID`. The anonymous user@host works but only warns.
exit 0
>>> notes member-out --project demo 
Observed, not verified: Claude Code refuses a subagent's Write of a report file, so a member's OUT files can be missing; the report then comes in its final message. A run with no report in OUT: suspect it first.
exit 0
>>> notes session-model --project demo 
Your own session model is chosen in Claude Code (`/model` or settings), not by qargi.
exit 0
>>> notes skills-dir --project demo 
Claude Code loads a checkout's skills from `.claude/skills` and the user's from `~/.claude/skills`; a session started with the launch line that qargi prints (`claude --add-dir DIR`) loads those of DIR too. To hide a skill without removing it, set {"skillOverrides": {"NAME": "off"}} in a settings file (user, project or project-local); qargi only reads those files.
exit 0
>>> notes spawn --project demo 
Start a member with the Agent tool: `subagent_type` is the member's name, `model` is the alias that `qargi agent for` prints (omit it when it prints `-`) and `effort` is the effort it prints. The call's model and effort override the member definition, so pass both.
exit 0
