>>> notes skills-dir --project demo --lead-runtime codex
Codex loads a checkout's skills from `.agents/skills` and the user's from `~/.codex/skills` (`CODEX_HOME/skills`) and `~/.agents/skills` (a directory with a SKILL.md each; a linked directory works); `install.sh --user --runtime codex` links qargi's skills into `~/.codex/skills`. To hide a skill without removing it, add an entry to `skills.config` in `~/.codex/config.toml` that names it with `enabled = false`; qargi only reads that file. Managed member snapshots default off. With the owner gate, canonical skills reaching the actual role are copied into private CODEX_HOME/skills; this destination declaration does not qualify loading or change capability dates. Committed checkout skills and readable files retain independent discovery/access behavior; prose grants no permissions.
exit 0
